<h2 id="faqs">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<div style="margin-bottom: 20px;">
    <h3 style="color: #0A2F5C; font-size: 1.15rem;">1. How do I find a good gynecologist doctor in Chhattisgarh?</h3>
    <p>Check for an MS or MD in Obstetrics and Gynaecology plus any surgical fellowship, confirm the same doctor will see you at every visit, ask whether the hospital can perform an emergency caesarean at any hour with blood and newborn care on site, and insist on written costs before treatment begins.</p>
</div>
<div style="margin-bottom: 20px;">
    <h3 style="color: #0A2F5C; font-size: 1.15rem;">2. Which city in Chhattisgarh has the most gynecologists?</h3>
    <p>Raipur, as the state capital, has the widest choice and the largest tertiary hospitals, followed by Bilaspur and Durg-Bhilai. Ambikapur is the main centre for the northern districts, serving Surguja, Surajpur, Balrampur, Jashpur and Korea.</p>
</div>
<div style="margin-bottom: 20px;">
    <h3 style="color: #0A2F5C; font-size: 1.15rem;">3. Where should women in Surguja district go for specialist care?</h3>
    <p>Ambikapur, the district headquarters, is the practical centre. Block-level health centres in Lundra, Sitapur, Lakhanpur, Batauli, Mainpat and Udaipur handle routine antenatal care and normal deliveries, with referral to Ambikapur for anything that needs a specialist.</p>
</div>
<div style="margin-bottom: 20px;">
    <h3 style="color: #0A2F5C; font-size: 1.15rem;">4. Is it worth travelling to another district for treatment?</h3>
    <p>For routine antenatal care, no. It is worth travelling for a second opinion before a hysterectomy if you may want children, when open surgery is advised without discussion of a keyhole option, when IVF is suggested before basic tests, or for a problem that has not improved despite treatment.</p>
</div>
<div style="margin-bottom: 20px;">
    <h3 style="color: #0A2F5C; font-size: 1.15rem;">5. How much does a gynecologist consultation cost in Chhattisgarh?</h3>
    <p>Private consultations generally range from 300 to 800 rupees, with Raipur at the upper end and follow-ups usually lower than the first visit. Scans and tests are billed separately and an estimate should be given in advance.</p>
</div>
<div style="margin-bottom: 20px;">
    <h3 style="color: #0A2F5C; font-size: 1.15rem;">6. Why is sickle cell screening important in this state?</h3>
    <p>Chhattisgarh has one of the highest burdens of the sickle cell gene in India. Sickle cell disease makes a pregnancy high-risk, and if both parents carry the trait the baby can inherit the disease. Screening is a simple blood test offered under the national elimination mission.</p>
</div>
<div style="margin-bottom: 20px;">
    <h3 style="color: #0A2F5C; font-size: 1.15rem;">7. What pregnancy care is free in Chhattisgarh?</h3>
    <p>Antenatal checkups, blood tests and ultrasound at government facilities, iron and folic acid under Anaemia Mukt Bharat, calcium supplements, the 75 g glucose test, sickle cell screening, institutional delivery support and ambulance transport.</p>
</div>
<div style="margin-bottom: 20px;">
    <h3 style="color: #0A2F5C; font-size: 1.15rem;">8. Where does Dr. Ankita Bansal Goyal consult?</h3>
    <p>At Sankalp Hospital, Bilaspur Road, behind District Hospital, Ambikapur, Chhattisgarh 497001, Monday to Saturday, 9:00 AM to 5:00 PM, with obstetric emergencies attended round the clock. Call or WhatsApp 096912 12570.</p>
</div>

