        {"@type":"Question","name":"Why is sickle cell screening important in Chhattisgarh?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Chhattisgarh has one of the highest burdens of the sickle cell gene in India. Sickle cell disease makes a pregnancy high-risk, and if both parents carry the trait the baby can inherit the disease. Screening is a simple blood test offered under the national elimination mission."}},
        {"@type":"Question","name":"What pregnancy care is free in Chhattisgarh?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Antenatal checkups, blood tests and ultrasound at government facilities, iron and folic acid under Anaemia Mukt Bharat, calcium supplements, the 75 g glucose test, sickle cell screening, institutional delivery support and ambulance transport."}},
        {"@type":"Question","name":"Where does Dr. Ankita Bansal Goyal consult?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"At Sankalp Hospital, Bilaspur Road, behind District Hospital, Ambikapur, Chhattisgarh 497001, Monday to Saturday, 9:00 AM to 5:00 PM, with obstetric emergencies attended round the clock. Call or WhatsApp 096912 12570."}}
      ]
    }
  ]
}
